From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 22:27:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: find the encoder through the atomic state, not
 encoder->crtc

get_encoder_from_crtc() walks every encoder looking for the legacy
encoder->crtc back-pointer. That field is maintained for compatibility and
is not the atomic source of truth, so the lookup returns NULL whenever it
has not been set up -- and both callers are vblank hooks that DRM may call
around a modeset:

  [drm:dpu_crtc_get_vblank_counter [msm]] *ERROR* no encoder found for crtc 0
  [drm:dpu_crtc_get_scanout_position [msm]] *ERROR* no encoder found for crtc 0

Ten of those on a Pixel 2 XL in a couple of hours of ordinary use. The
failure is not free: dpu_crtc_get_vblank_counter() returns 0 on this path,
which makes the vblank counter appear to jump backwards, and
dpu_crtc_get_scanout_position() reports no position so vblank timestamps
fall back to an estimate.

Every other encoder lookup in this file already iterates
crtc->state->encoder_mask. Do the same here, and guard the case where the
CRTC has no state at all.

A disabled CRTC legitimately has no encoder, so the message becomes
DRM_DEBUG_KMS rather than DRM_ERROR: it is a transient state, not a driver
error.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c | 13 +++++++------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
index d959b7dc12a2..0401c46b8cc6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -53,12 +53,13 @@ static struct dpu_kms *_dpu_crtc_get_kms(struct drm_crtc *crtc)
 
 static struct drm_encoder *get_encoder_from_crtc(struct drm_crtc *crtc)
 {
-	struct drm_device *dev = crtc->dev;
 	struct drm_encoder *encoder;
 
-	drm_for_each_encoder(encoder, dev)
-		if (encoder->crtc == crtc)
-			return encoder;
+	if (!crtc->state)
+		return NULL;
+
+	drm_for_each_encoder_mask(encoder, crtc->dev, crtc->state->encoder_mask)
+		return encoder;
 
 	return NULL;
 }
@@ -189,7 +190,7 @@ static u32 dpu_crtc_get_vblank_counter(struct drm_crtc *crtc)
 {
 	struct drm_encoder *encoder = get_encoder_from_crtc(crtc);
 	if (!encoder) {
-		DRM_ERROR("no encoder found for crtc %d\n", crtc->index);
+		DRM_DEBUG_KMS("no encoder found for crtc %d\n", crtc->index);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
@@ -279,7 +280,7 @@ static bool dpu_crtc_get_scanout_position(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 
 	encoder = get_encoder_from_crtc(crtc);
 	if (!encoder) {
-		DRM_ERROR("no encoder found for crtc %d\n", pipe);
+		DRM_DEBUG_KMS("no encoder found for crtc %d\n", pipe);
 		return false;
 	}
 
